\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Wick powers with a variance parameter}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Over a commutative ring, define polynomials in #{z} with parameter
#{s} recursively by
##{W_0(z;s)=1,\qquad
W_{n+1}(z;s)=zW_n(z;s)-s\,\partial_zW_n(z;s).}
The derivative is the formal polynomial derivative. The
\newvocab{Wick power} of degree #{n} with parameter #{s} is
##{{:z^n:}_s=W_n(z;s).}
This definition uses finitely many polynomial operations for each
#{n}. In the Gaussian applications the ring is #{\RR} and
#{s\ge0} is the specified variance.}

\p{The recursion is the declaration
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.hermiteHeat}. Its variance-one specialization
is the probabilists' Hermite normalization used in
\ref{fdip-007U}. This polynomial definition supplies neither a
Gaussian probability nor a conditional-expectation map.}
